  "title": "UN Human Rights Council Review Dismissed Amid US Policy Shift",
  "summary": "The Trump administration's decision to boycott the UN Human Rights Council's regular review, citing concerns about its bias toward Israel and its policies, marks a significant change in the organization's approach to human rights oversight.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "The U.S. State Department denied entry visas for the Palestinian delegation to the UN General Assembly for the forum.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The UN Security Council and IAEA have both refused to address Iran's nuclear non-compliance claims.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The U.S. administration has set a new policy to fully exclude its participation in the UN Human Rights Council since it was established two decades ago.",
      "confidence": 0.95
